An operations dashboard provides administrators with a centralized view of the health and performance of Azure resources. By consolidating critical operational metrics into one interface, teams can identify issues more quickly and make informed decisions.

A useful dashboard may display:

* Resource health
* Active alerts
* CPU and memory utilization
* Network performance
* Backup status
* Security recommendations
* Cost summaries
* Service availability

# Real-Life Example:
For example, an operations engineer can review the dashboard each morning to verify that production systems remain healthy before users begin their workday.

# Real-Life Use Case:
A real-life use case is Network Operations Centers (NOCs) monitoring hundreds of cloud workloads simultaneously.

A centralized dashboard improves visibility, response time, and operational efficiency.
